# Graphify mandatory (orchestrator)

Full workflow: [docs/GRAPHIFY_WORKFLOW.md](../../docs/GRAPHIFY_WORKFLOW.md).

## Before any code edit session

1. Run **`scripts/graphify_gate.ps1 -Query "..."`** (or `bash scripts/graphify_gate.sh '...'` on CHI404) — records consult in `graphify-out/.last-graph-query.json`.
2. Run **`scripts/graphify_pre_edit.ps1`** — fails (exit 2) if gate stamp missing or older than 4 hours.
3. **Consult the graph output** before locating or editing code:
   - Prefer `graphify query` / `graphify path` / `graphify explain` over blind repo-wide grep.
   - CHI404 / R|Trader: read [docs/vault/CHI404_CANONICAL_ENTRYPOINTS.md](../../docs/vault/CHI404_CANONICAL_ENTRYPOINTS.md) after graph query.
4. Do not start builder/investigator edit work until graph gate + context are loaded.

## After any code edits

1. Rebuild: `graphify update .` or `scripts/graphify_rebuild.ps1` from repo root (AST-only; **no Google API**).
2. Optional semantic PDF/docs pass: `scripts/graphify_semantic_local.ps1` (local Ollama, not Gemini).
3. Commit updated `graphify-out/` artifacts with the code change when the team tracks graph in git.

Orchestrator owns pre-edit consult and post-edit rebuild; subagents receive graph context from the main thread.
